# Keep the build context lean and stable. Mirrors .gitignore plus VCS,
# IDE, and tooling state that must never enter the image or perturb cache keys.

# Version control / hooks
.git
.githooks
.github

# IDE / editor / agent state
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.codex
# .erun/config.yaml is checked into git (the repo's own project config) and
# TestProjectConfigPinsAmd64OnlyPlatformsForConfirmedAmd64Environments reads
# it inside the erun-devops image's cli-test stage, so it is carved out with the same
# ".erun/*" plus negation shape ProjectConfigGitIgnoreFix documents for
# .gitignore -- a bare ".erun" exclusion cannot be un-excluded per file
# (docker cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded).
.erun/*
!.erun/config.yaml
# Root .gitignore excludes this unanchored (any depth); computeBuildFingerprint
# (erun-common/build_incremental.go) honours nested .gitignores too, so a
# macOS checkout that leaves one of these under a COPYd module would enter the
# real build context without moving the fingerprint unless mirrored here.
**/.DS_Store

# Same asymmetry, for the two things `terraform init` writes into the module
# tree it initializes: the module guides tell a developer to run `terraform
# test` by hand in a module under erun-devops/terraform-erun. Root .gitignore
# excludes both unanchored at any depth, so the fingerprint already ignores them; without these rules the real
# build context would still carry ~105MB of provider binaries per initialized
# module for a file the fingerprint never sees.
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Go build artifacts and test output
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
__debug_bin*
.gomodcache

# Integration-suite local artifacts (regenerated per run; must not enter the
# build context or perturb fingerprint cache keys)
/erun-integration/coverage
/erun-integration/bin

# eslint/prettier --cache output; never COPYd into a build context, mirrored
# here only for hygiene
/.cache/

# Local packaging / release artifacts
/erun-devops/linux/*/dist
/erun-cli/bin

# Desktop UI build outputs. /erun-ui/frontend/wailsjs is the one exception
# to "not consumed by service Dockerfiles": the erun-ui build stage
# regenerates it in-image with `go tool wails generate module` before
# typechecking/building erun-ui/frontend, so a possibly-stale host copy must never leak into the build context.
/erun-ui/bin
/erun-ui/build/bin
# The macOS app bundle and the darwin build tree a local desktop build leaves
# beside the module (excluded only by a clone's own .git/info/exclude, which
# neither docker nor the fingerprint reads): ~90MB of host binaries no Linux
# build consumes, which would bloat every context that COPYs erun-ui and move
# its fingerprint on every local desktop build.
/erun-ui/ERun.app
/erun-ui/darwin
/erun-ui/frontend/node_modules
/erun-ui/frontend/dist
/erun-ui/frontend/wailsjs
/erun-ui/frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
/erun-ui/frontend/package.json.md5
/erun-ui/playwright/node_modules
/erun-ui/playwright/test-results
/erun-ui/playwright/playwright-report
/erun-ui/playwright/playwright/.cache
/erun-ui/.golangci-cache

# Root yarn workspace (erun-kit, erun-console, erun-ui/frontend): the
# erun-console and erun-ui Dockerfiles run `yarn install` in-image, so hoisted
# deps and build outputs are regenerated there and must
# never enter the build context — the workspace root node_modules alone is
# hundreds of MB, and its presence would diverge the context from the
# fingerprint the same way /erun-docs/node_modules would.
/node_modules
/erun-kit/node_modules
/erun-kit/dist
/erun-kit/.vite
/erun-kit/**/*.local
/erun-console/node_modules
/erun-console/dist
/erun-console/.vite
/erun-console/**/*.local
/erun-console/playwright/node_modules
/erun-console/playwright/test-results
/erun-console/playwright/playwright-report
/erun-console/playwright/.cache*
/erun-devops/e2e/*/node_modules
/erun-devops/e2e/*/test-results
/erun-devops/e2e/*/playwright-report

# Docs site dependencies and build outputs. The erun-docs image runs
# `yarn install` + `yarn build` inside its Dockerfile, so these are
# regenerated in-image and must never enter the build context: they bloat it
# (~1GB of node_modules alone) and, because the build only honours this root
# .dockerignore while the fingerprint also honours erun-docs/.gitignore, their
# presence diverges the real context from the fingerprint.
/erun-docs/node_modules
/erun-docs/build
/erun-docs/.docusaurus
/erun-docs/.cache-loader

# Env files
.env
